---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout pageName="Persona">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="center">Behind all of this!</h2>
    <section>
      <p>
        Well, hi! I'm not sure why you're here, and even less sure why you'd
        want to read about me, but... if you do, who am I to stop you? So, hi
        again! I'm Pavel, and this is my space that I created as part of my
        portfolio and as a personal area to store my projects and ideas, and to
        share them with my friends in a way that's more than just sending links.
        As a person who loves to create, I've always been drawn to finding the
        perfect medium for me. I've tried everything, but none of them gave me
        the creative freedom I needed, as none of them fully reflected my
        vision. So, I try to combine different mediums, and programming has
        allowed me to truly create what I want! I love storytelling, whether
        through images, sounds, or plain narrative, and programming lets me
        bring it all together into one great interactive adventure. Given all
        this, it's no surprise that my goal became game development and creating
        my own worlds. However, I don't limit myself to just that. I find joy
        and excitement in making "something out of nothing," whether it's a
        game, a program, or a website. Through my learning journey, I discovered
        that my true passion and relaxation come not necessarily from creating
        games, but from developing game engines. I love the idea of creating
        tools that can express visions. Additionally, as someone who appreciates
        knowledge and science, I enjoy the ability to replicate real-world
        phenomena in the digital realm. If you'd like to stick around and check
        out my projects, go ahead and WELCOME! :)
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h3>Why JS?</h3>
      <p>
        That's a great question! Was it coincidence, or maybe just sheer luck?
        When I first decided to try coding, I found it difficult to locate any
        tutorials that interested me. I wasn't excited about the idea of
        learning by simply adding two numbers and then subtracting them, just to
        console.log a bunch of values. I knew that if I was going to do this, I
        needed to find a way that was interesting to me! After days of
        searching, I stumbled across a YouTube channel called The Coding Train.
        Daniel was teaching JavaScript in a really interactive way—by creating
        shapes on the screen, animating them, and making them collide. It was
        just the fun and engaging experience I needed to spark my interest and
        keep me on track! And that’s it! That’s why I chose JavaScript. A few
        years later, here I am, and I would make the same choice all over again.
        I’ve fallen in love with JS and the idea of developing for the web.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h3 class="center">So what now?</h3>
      <p>
        Now, I just want to do what I love. I code both as my job and as my
        hobby, and I'm deeply immersed in this world with the hope of one day
        telling my own stories through my games and projects. Feel free to reach
        out and ask me anything you’d like to know more about. You can find my
        social media links on the main page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style lang="scss">
  @import "../styles/vars.scss";
  .wrap {
    padding: 4rem 4rem;
    @media (max-width: $midScreen) {
      padding: 3rem 3rem;
    }
    @media (max-width: $smallScreen) {
      padding: 2rem 2rem;
    }
  }
  p {
    color: $primaryColor;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: bold;
    @media (max-width: $midScreen) {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }
  section {
  }

  .center {
    text-align: center;
  }
  h3,
  h2 {
    font-weight: bold;
    color: $secondaryColor;
    font-size: 3rem;
    padding-top: 5rem;
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
    @media (max-width: $midScreen) {
      font-size: 2.5rem;
    }
    @media (max-width: $smallScreen) {
      font-size: 2rem;
      padding-top: 2rem;
      padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
